  "text": "capture\n\nA captured payment.\n\nstatus\nenum\nOptional\nThe status of the captured payment.\nValue in\n\"COMPLETED\" | \"DECLINED\" | \"PARTIALLY_REFUNDED\" | \"PENDING\" | \"REFUNDED\" | \"FAILED\"\nstatus_details\nobject<capture_status_details>\nOptional\nThe details of the captured payment status.\nid\nstring\nOptional\nThe PayPal-generated ID for the captured payment.\nMatch\n^[\\S\\s]*$\nLength\n0 <= length <= 2147483647\namount\nobject<amount_with_breakdown>\nOptional\nThe total order amount with an optional breakdown that provides details, such as the total item amount, total tax amount, shipping, handling, insurance, and discounts, if any.\nIf you specify `amount.breakdown`, the amount equals `item_total` plus `tax_total` plus `shipping` plus `handling` plus `insurance` minus `shipping_discount` minus discount.\nThe amount must be a positive number. For listed of supported currencies and decimal precision, see the PayPal REST APIs Currency Codes.\ninvoice_id\nstring\nOptional\nThe API caller-provided external invoice number for this order. Appears in both the payer's transaction history and the emails that the payer receives.\nMatch\n^[\\S\\s]*$\nLength\n0 <= length <= 2147483647\ncustom_id\nstring\nOptional\nThe API caller-provided external ID. Used to reconcile API caller-initiated transactions with PayPal transactions. Appears in transaction and settlement reports.\nMatch\n^[\\S\\s]*$\nLength\n0 <= length <= 255\nnetwork_transaction_reference\nobject<network_transaction>\nOptional\nReference values used by the card network to identify a transaction.\nseller_protection\nobject<seller_protection>\nOptional\nThe level of protection offered as defined by [PayPal Seller Protection for Merchants](https://www.paypal.com/us/webapps/mpp/security/seller-protection).\nfinal_capture\nboolean\nOptional\nIndicates whether you can make additional captures against the authorized payment. Set to `true` if you do not intend to capture additional payments against the authorization. Set to `false` if you intend to capture additional payments against the authorization.\nDefault\nfalse\nseller_receivable_breakdown\nobject<seller_receivable_breakdown>\nOptional\nThe detailed breakdown of the capture activity. This is not available for transactions that are in pending state.\ndisbursement_mode\nenum<disbursement_mode>\nOptional\nThe funds that are held on behalf of the merchant.\nDefault\n\"INSTANT\"\nValue in\n\"INSTANT\" | \"DELAYED\"\nlinks\nobject<link_description-2>[]\nOptional\nAn array of related [HATEOAS links](/docs/api/reference/api-responses/#hateoas-links).\nItems\n0 <= length <= 32767\nprocessor_response\nobject<processor_response>\nOptional\nThe processor response information for payment requests, such as direct credit card transactions.\ncreate_time\nstring<date_time>\nOptional\nThe date and time, in [Internet date and time format](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3339#section-5.6). Seconds are required while fractional seconds are optional.\nNote: The regular expression provides guidance but does not reject all invalid dates.\nMatch\n^[0-9]{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[1-2][0-9]|3[0-1])[T,t]([0-1][0-9]|2[0-3]):[0-5][0-9]:([0-5][0-9]|60)([.][0-9]+)?([Zz]|[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})$\nLength\n20 <= length <= 64\nupdate_time\nstring<date_time>\nOptional\nThe date and time, in [Internet date and time format](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3339#section-5.6). Seconds are required while fractional seconds are optional.\nNote: The regular expression provides guidance but does not reject all invalid dates.\nMatch\n^[0-9]{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[1-2][0-9]|3[0-1])[T,t]([0-1][0-9]|2[0-3]):[0-5][0-9]:([0-5][0-9]|60)([.][0-9]+)?([Zz]|[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})$\nLength\n20 <= length <= 64",
  "title": "capture - Payments v2 | PayPal Developer",
  "url": "https://developer.paypal.com/api/payments/v2/definitions/capture"
}
